.TH CHTTP_BASE64_ENCODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_encode \- encode a buffer as base64 (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

char *chttp_base64_encode(const void *data, size_t len,
                          size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper around chttp_base64_encode_mp(). It
gives NULL for the memory management procedures, so the function uses
malloc and free.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
data     The buffer to encode. It can be NULL only if len is 0.
len      The number of bytes in data.
out_len  Optional. It gets the length of the string that the function
         gives back. This length does not count the terminating NUL.
         Give NULL to ignore it.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new base64 string that ends with a NUL, if the call succeeds.
NULL, if the allocation fails. NULL also, if data is NULL and len is
not zero. NULL also, if len is so large that the encoded size
overflows size_t.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_encode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_decode (3)
